+---
+id: task-001-implement-json-pointer-resolution-rfc-6901
+type: task
+title: "Implement JSON Pointer resolution (RFC 6901)"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Implement JSON Pointer resolution (RFC 6901)
+
+Our services need a standard way to refer to a value inside a JSON document. Implement JSON Pointer,
+as specified in RFC 6901, as the first building block that later features will build on.
+
+## Requirements
+
+- Export a function `resolvePointer(document, pointer)` from `src/index.ts`.
+- Given a JSON document and a JSON Pointer string, return the value the pointer refers to.
+- Throw an error when the pointer is not a valid JSON Pointer (RFC 6901 section 3 syntax: the empty
+  string, or a string starting with `/`; `~` only appears as `~0` or `~1`).
+- Throw an error when the pointer does not resolve to a value of the document (missing member, array
+  index out of range, a non-canonical array index such as a leading zero or `-`, or stepping into a
+  scalar).
+- Unescape reference tokens in the RFC order: `~1` to `/` first, then `~0` to `~`.
+- The empty pointer `""` refers to the whole document.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+- Happy path: `""` returns the whole document; `/a/b`, array indices, and `~0` / `~1` escapes resolve
+  to the expected values, including the RFC 6901 example document.
+- Error path: an invalid pointer (for example `a`, `/a~2`) throws.
+- Error path: a missing key, an out-of-range or non-canonical array index, and a path through a scalar
+  throw.
+- Tests run with `node --test` (the `test` script in `package.json`), deterministically, without
+  external services.
+
+## Notes
+
+- The package has no runtime dependency; keep it that way.
+- The project is in TypeScript (`tsconfig.json`, `strict`); give the public function explicit types.
